-10-31 and whose term 1 is 2026-11-01 to 2027-10-31 for 365.00. These tests are red now only because the stub's PolicyResponse has no endDate or terms (PolicyResponse.cs:4-10). A stub canned from the contract example would turn them green without computing any end date. The same cause is in I4, I5 and I6, but each is reported against its own rule. The other SELL-3 tests (:51-60 1 Mar 2027, :65-75 29 Feb 2028) use non-default starts, so they do discriminate. Rule: 'End date = start + 1 year − 1 day, calculated, cover inclusive.'</dd></div><div class="kit-finding-card__field"><dt>Files</dt><dd><a class="kit-file-line-link__link" href="https://github.com/dpmorgandev/uinsure-policies-api/blob/main/tests/Uinsure.Policies.Api.Tests/SellTermLengthTests.cs" aria-label="tests/Uinsure.Policies.Api.Tests/SellTermLengthTests.cs on GitHub" data-line="absent" data-comp="file-line-link · primitive · line absent"><span class="kit-file-line-link__text">tests/Uinsure.Policies.Api.Tests/SellTermLengthTests.cs</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-external-link kit-file-line-link__icon" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M15 3h6v6"></path><path d="M10 14 21 3"></path><path d="M18 13v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6"></path></svg></a> <a class="kit-file-line-link__link" href="https://github.com/dpmorgandev/uinsure-policies-api/blob/main/tests/Uinsure.Policies.Api.Tests/Builders/SellPolicyRequestBuilder.cs" aria-label="tests/Uinsure.Policies.Api.Tests/Builders/SellPolicyRequestBuilder.cs on GitHub" data-line="absent" data-comp="file-line-link · primitive · line absent"><span class="kit-file-line-link__text">tests/Uinsure.Policies.Api.Tests/Builders/SellPolicyRequestBuilder.cs</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentCol