+<article class="kit-finding-card__card" aria-labelledby="fc-d2-i11" data-testable="true" data-fixed="true" data-comp="finding-card · project · testable"><h3 id="fc-d2-i11" class="kit-finding-card__title"><span class="kit-finding-card__id">I11</span><span class="kit-status-tag__tag kit-status-tag__pass" data-status="pass"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-check kit-status-tag__icon" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"></path></svg><span>Fixed</span></span><span class="kit-finding-card__testable"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-flask-conical kit-finding-card__icon" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M14 2v6a2 2 0 0 0 .245.96l5.51 10.08A2 2 0 0 1 18 22H6a2 2 0 0 1-1.755-2.96l5.51-10.08A2 2 0 0 0 10 8V2"></path><path d="M6.453 15h11.094"></path><path d="M8.5 2h7"></path></svg><span>Testable</span></span></h3><dl class="kit-finding-card__fields"><div class="kit-finding-card__field"><dt>Symptom</dt><dd>This is a separate cause from I9 and I10. The harness bar was raised by PR #8: D2's previous_attempts judged these tests 'discriminating', and under the old bar they were. thirteen success tests (counting the 1 Mar and 29 Feb tests separately) sell builder defaults for every field except the one under test, and read back only that one field or two. The rows: SELL-2 at today (SellStartDateWindowTests.cs:23-31, startDate only at :30), today+60 (:35-43, :42), BST UK date (:95-104, :103) and GMT (:109-118, :117); SELL-3 1 Mar 2027 (SellTermLengthTests.cs:71-80, endDate only at :79) and 29 Feb 2028 (:85-95, :93-94); SELL-5 16th birthday on the start date (SellPolicyholderAgeTests.cs:25-37, dateOfBirth only at :36); SELL-6 full amount (SellPaymentTests.cs:21-32, payment only at :28-31) and two different references (:74-84, :81-83); SELL-7 one penny (SellAmountTests.cs:22-30, amount only at :29); the round-trip buy-to-let plumbing test (SellRoundTripTests.cs:52-62, :60-61); and the shape postcode-of-8 row (SellShapeTests.cs:180-191, :190).</dd></div><div class="kit-finding-card__field"><dt>Cause</dt><dd>none of them calls the shared SoldPolicyAssert.ReadsBackAsSold (SoldPolicyAssert.cs:14). So the stored type, dates, amount, autoRenew, property, holders, term 1 and payment are never compared with the request. While I9 and I10 stand, the unchecked fields are also the example values. Rule: 'Full read-back for every success test. One shared assertion compares the whole read-back to the request sent (every field the node's response carries) … Derived values (end date, refund) are literals from the test'.</dd></div><div class="kit-finding-card__field"><dt>Files</dt><dd><a class="kit-file-line-link__link" href="https://github.com/dpmorgandev/uinsure-policies-api/blob/main/tests/Uinsure.Policies.Api.Tests/SellStartDateWindowTests.cs" aria-label="tests/Uinsure.Policies.Api.Tests/SellStartDateWindowTests.cs on GitHub" data-line="absent" data-comp="file-line-link · primitive · line absent"><span class="kit-file-line-link__text">tests/Uinsure.Policies.Api.Tests/SellStartDateWindowTests.cs</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-external-link kit-file-line-link__icon" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M15 3h6v6"></path><path d="M10 14 21 3"></path><path d="M18 13v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6"></path></svg></a> <a class="kit-file-line-link__link" href="https://github.com/dpmorgandev/uinsure-policies-api/blob/main/tests/Uinsure.Policies.Api.Tests/SellTermLengthTests.cs" aria-label="tests/