+{"schema_version":1,"plan_id":"ui","node_id":"U8","attempt":2,"source":"reviewer","source_ref":"docs/trace/ui/U8/verdicts/A1-reviewer.json R1, R2 (P1), R3, R4 (P2); docs/trace/ui/U8/verdicts/A1-security.json (PASS; note 58 is the same publish race as R1)","findings":[{"id":"I1","rule_id":"WB-7","layer":"api","files":["src/web/app/workbench/browser.ts","src/web/app/data/api.ts","tests/web/unit/client/wb-7-log-growth.test.tsx"],"root_cause":"Reviewer R1, and the security verdict's note at A1-security.json:58 (one cause, two reports). Layer note: this is the ui client layer, not the C# API; 'api' follows the W3 A1/I5 convention. Symptom: the request log can show an exchange with a status but no response body. That breaks WB-7 ('the exact request and response') and HONEST-1. It also drops the selling POST from the policy view's sale match, because that match reads responseBody (src/web/app/workbench/policy/PolicyView.tsx:340). Cause: publish() treats an exchange as settled when its status is non-null and then reuses that object for good (src/web/app/workbench/browser.ts:25). But loggingFetch settles an entry in three steps with an await in the middle. It sets status (src/web/app/data/api.ts:440) and headers (:441), then awaits response.clone().text() before it sets responseBody (:442). A publish() from another request, on its send (browser.ts:32) or its finally (:36), can land in that await. When it does, it takes a shallow copy holding status and headers but responseBody null. The entry's own final publish then keeps that stale copy (browser.ts:25), so the body never reaches any snapshot. The status test is the wrong marker of 'settled': settled has to mean the body has been read too. The test missed it because wb-7-log-growth.test.tsx:37 awaits each fetch in turn, so no publish ever falls inside another exchange's body read. Recurrence: this is a new fingerprint, but attempt 1's own route introduced it (diff.patch:9784-9788, green 8148181). That route was the fix for W3 A4 I9 (W4|src/web/app/workbench/browser.ts|unbounded-log-full-copy-per-publish). The fix removed the per-publish copy and keyed reuse on a field that is set before the entry is complete. So I9's cause is closed, and its fix opened this one. Fix direction: count an exchange as settled for reuse only once every field loggingFetch writes is in place, the body included. Or make loggingFetch complete the entry in one step after the body read. Then add a test with two exchanges in flight at once.","fingerprint":"WB-7|src/web/app/workbench/browser.ts|settled-on-status-before-body-read","testable":true,"suggested_test":"Given the global fetch stubbed so that exchange A's response body is a stream the test holds open, and exchange B's answers at once. When A is sent and has its status, B is sent and answered while A's body is still unread, and then A's body is released and A settles. Then the request log the page reads holds A with its status and with responseBody equal to the exact text released, and the policy view's sale match would find A's reference in it. (tests/web/unit/client/wb-7-log-concurrent.test.tsx, beside wb-7-log-growth.test.tsx, WB-7 · prefix)","untestable_reason":null},{"id":"I2","rule_id":"WB-5","layer":"api","files":["src/web/app/workbench/renew/RenewPolicy.tsx","src/web/app/data/api.ts","src/web/kit/primitives/money-input/MoneyInput.tsx"],"root_cause":"Reviewer R2. Layer note: ui screen layer, with 'api' per the convention. Symptom: acceptance line 9b (docs/plans/active/ui.dag.yaml:462) wants the 'amount null' renewal explained or fixed in RenewPolicy. The node's only trace of it is gate.red's 'amount-null not reproducible' (docs/trace/ui/U8/loop.jsonl:3), and the diff doesn't touch the amount path. Cause, which is deterministic and not intermittent: submit sends Number(amount) with no check (src/web/app/workbench/renew/RenewPolicy.tsx:91). The field is the kit MoneyInput, a free text input that parses nothing on entry (src/web/kit/primitives/money-input/MoneyInput.tsx:8-9, :19). So any text Number() can't read, such as '12,50', '£100' or a doubled default like '100.00100.00', becomes NaN. postJson's JSON.stringify (src/web/app/data/api.ts:413) then writes NaN as null. RenewalRequest.amount is typed number (api.ts:394), so the page can't send the typed text as it was typed. That conflicts with MoneyInput's own contract that 'the rules are the API's'. An empty field also goes out as 0, a value nobody typed (HONEST-1). What put non-numeric text in the field during W3's single failing run is still unknown. The mechanism that turns any such text into null is the line above, and it can be reproduced at will. Recurrence: this was carried from W3 A4 I6 (WB-5|tests/web/e2e/W3/wb-5.spec.ts|cheque-test-types-before-read-amount-null-intermittent). Attempt 1 fixed that fingerprint's test half (9a, met per the reviewer's note). It treated the code half as 'not reproducible' because it looked for the intermittent trigger and didn't explain the deterministic conversion I6 named. The code-side cause gets its own fingerprint here, so this is not a repeat of I6's. Fix direction: RenewPolicy must stop sending an invented null or 0 for an amount nobody gave. Either the form refuses a non-numeric or empty amount before sending and says why, or the client sends the typed text exactly so the API's own 400 answers it. The choice and its reason go into the trail, which explains line 9b as well as fixing it. David may want to rule between the two, since one adds a check in the UI.","fingerprint":"WB-5|src/web/app/workbench/renew/RenewPolicy.tsx|unchecked-number-amount-sent-as-null","testable":true,"suggested_test":"Given the renew screen after the policy read has answered, with a stub fetch. When the person replaces the amount with 'abc', or clears it, and presses Renew policy. Then no request body {\"amount\":null} or {\"amount\":0} is sent: either no POST goes out and the field says why, or the POST body carries the text as typed. (tests/web/unit/screens/wb-5-renew-amount.test.tsx, WB-5 · prefix)","untestable_reason":null},{"id":"I3","rule_id":"A11Y-1","layer":"tests","files":["docs/trace/ui/U8/loop.jsonl","tests/web/e2e/U8/a11y-1.spec.ts"],"root_cause":"Reviewer R3. This is an orchestrator receipt and needs no code change. It shouldn't go to the tester, even though the verdict routes it there. Symptom: acceptance line docs/plans/active/ui.dag.yaml:456 names a gate.axe receipt, and loop.jsonl has none. Cause: the t6 gate run (ui.dag.yaml:473 lists axe as its own gate) ran the U8 e2e folder as a single gate.e2e (docs/trace/ui/U8/loop.jsonl:18, 'npx playwright test tests/web/e2e/U8', '14 passed'). The 7 A11Y-1 tests in tests/web/e2e/U8/a11y-1.spec.ts passed inside it, but no separate gate.axe event was written. The test half of W3 A4 I3 (A11Y-1|tests/web/e2e/W3|no-axe-for-new-routes) is closed, because the specs exist and pass. Only the receipt half is open, so this gets a new fingerprint. The earlier route didn't prevent it because the orchestrator's gate step counted the axe specs under gate.e2e and recorded no axe gate by name. Fix direction: the orchestrator runs the axe specs as their own gate on the next gate run and records a gate.axe event with its command, exit and count.","fingerprint":"A11Y-1|docs/trace/ui/U8/loop.jsonl|no-gate-axe-receipt","testable":false,"suggested_test":null,"untestable_reason":"This is a missing receipt in the orchestrator's loop.jsonl, not app or test behaviour. The axe tests already exist and pass (loop.jsonl:18), so no Given/When/Then can fail on it. The orchestrator closes it by recording the gate."},{"id":"I4","rule_id":"WB-5","layer":"api","files":["src/web/app/workbench/renew/RenewPolicy.tsx"],"root_cause":"Reviewer R4, first part. I've split R4's second point into I5 because it has a different cause. Symptom and cause are one line. termMethod has two JSDoc blocks in a row (src/web/app/workbench/renew/RenewPolicy.tsx:19 and :20), and only the last one attaches to the function, so :19 documents nothing. Origin: attempt 1's green 8148181 added the HONEST-1 block at :20 (diff.patch:9865) above the old one-line block without merging the two (code-quality slop list: stale comments). Recurrence: new fingerprint. It's the same kind of slip as W3 A4 I8, where a fix left an orphan comment behind (orphan-nav-settle-comment), but it's a different file and cause. Fix direction: make the two blocks one doc comment that says both what the method is and when it's null.","fingerprint":"WB-5|src/web/app/workbench/renew/RenewPolicy.tsx|orphan-termmethod-jsdoc","testable":false,"suggested_test":null,"untestable_reason":"A doc comment isn't app behaviour, so no Given/When/Then can detect it. Review checks it."},{"id":"I5","rule_id":"HONEST-1","layer":"api","files":["src/web/app/workbench/renew/RenewPolicy.tsx"],"root_cause":"Reviewer R4, second point, which the reviewer gave as 'a related minor point'. I've split it from I4 because its cause is different. Symptom: the payment method hint always reads 'Defaults from term N' (src/web/app/workbench/renew/RenewPolicy.tsx:154), even when termMethod returns null and the Select shows its 'None returned for the term' placeholder (:75, :156). Cause: the hint text is fixed and doesn't depend on whether a default was found. Attempt 1 changed the null case to show no default (8148181) but left the hint untouched, so the screen claims a default it doesn't have, which HONEST-1 forbids. Recurrence: new fingerprint. Attempt 1's 'no Card fallback' change made it visible. Fix direction: the hint names a default only when the read gave one. Otherwise it says the read named no method for the term.","fingerprint":"HONEST-1|src/web/app/workbench/renew/RenewPolicy.tsx|hint-claims-default-when-none","testable":true,"suggested_test":"Given an auto-renewing policy whose current term's paymentReference matches no payment in the read. When the renew screen renders after the read. Then the payment method field's hint doesn't say 'Defaults from term' and the Select shows its placeholder. (tests/web/unit/screens/wb-5-renew-method-hint.test.tsx, HONEST-1 · prefix)","untestable_reason":null}],"previous_attempts":["attempt 1: red 77b374c..95c2c3d, d1b3fae (gate.red: 9b 'amount-null not reproducible'); in-node kit gap 5d7cf21 (request-log pending); green 8148181; gates pass, regression deferred to U10; reviewer FAIL A1 (R1 P1 publish race, introduced by the W3 A4 I9 fix; R2 P1 amount-null, carried from W3 A4 I6 and only its test half fixed; R3 P2 gate.axe receipt missing, test half of W3 A4 I3 closed; R4 P2 orphan JSDoc); security PASS with R1's race in its notes"]}
